{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Landed: Gerrit 1941 merged as 13c7fe9ae1 with LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1, 0 unresolved. Orchestrator verified the landed change against origin/main independently: exactly four files (AGENTS.md +7, Makefile +19, scripts/amend_commit_message.py +185, tests/unit/test_amend_msg_change_id.py +261) and NO pre-push hook, reflog comparison, or other guard — the out-of-scope boundary held. AGENTS.md line 282 now names make amend-msg as the path for a rewritten message, cites the three duplicate changes this footgun produced today (1921, 1926, 1931), and documents the loud refusal when HEAD carries no Change-Id. The server-side rebase preserved Change-Id Ibb5fb5425d4635019302a4956a5cdc7071d7b84f — the same id the wrapper carried through its own dogfood amend, so the tool was validated end-to-end through a real Gerrit round-trip in addition to its fixture tests. Closing: the local full-suite run the implementing agent was waiting on is not the authoritative signal here — CI's Verified +1 ran the whole tree on the exact merged commit, and the local run was executing under concurrent interference from other sessions."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787199972282902001,"uuid":"d5188741-1790-45aa-8a0f-e445ec6d5ed6"}